        "original_id": "9d280d41-df8d-573c-8dcc-c0f61318114d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dave Peverett, Jimi Hendrix, Charlie Huhn, Bryan Bassett\n- Bands: Foghat, Savoy Brown\n- Albums: Family Joules\n- Concepts: dive bomb\n\nFacts:\n- Jimi Hendrix was born as Johnny Allen Hendrix on November 27, 1942, and he became an American rock guitarist, singer, and songwriter.\n- Dave Peverett was born on April 16, 1943, and he was an English singer and musician also known as Lonesome Dave.\n- Dave Peverett was the original lead vocalist and rhythm guitarist of Foghat, which he founded after his tenure in Savoy Brown.\n- Jimi Hendrix is recognized as one of the pioneers of the dive bomb guitar technique.\n- Jimi Hendrix died on September 18, 1970.\n- Family Joules was the first Foghat album without founding member Dave Peverett and the first to feature singer-guitarist Charlie Huhn and guitarist Bryan Bassett.\n- Dave Peverett died on February 7, 2000.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
